    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Ok, thanks. Looking at that Edge Computing section again—the policy drafts seem to imply that the transition to decentralized edge controllers will eventually phase out the need for the central Grid-Brain oversight. Can you run some simulations on how the grid stability would look if we transitioned to a mostly edge-based, decentralized management model? I want to see what the reliability delta is between current centralized control and the proposed decentralized architecture.",
