      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Running simulations on a decentralized edge-based management model has yielded mixed results. The Edge Controller Density (ECD) score - an indicator of the grid's stability and resilience - has seen an increment, averaging around 4.8% when considering edge workloads, shortening the critical time to re-route and resolve failures. Despite these gains, the simulations reveal a less reliable response to large-scale events where centralized oversight currently excels. Integrating edge-based decision protocols without the central Grid-Brain can risk greater than 3% in average service disruption during such events, indicating a reliability deficit of about 6-8% under extreme conditions compared to centralized control. Further refinement of balance mechanisms and a hybrid approach might yet yield better stability in a truly decentralized grid.",
